  {
    id: "merach-ultrawalk-w60",
    name: "MERACH UltraWalk W60",
    brand: "MERACH",
    category: "Most complete app and best-built pad",
    badge: "Best Overall",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H1WZJX6S?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41sUqeSw53L._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/merach-treadmills/",
    priceRange: "About $282 (Amazon, 24 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":282,"high":282},
    specs: "MERACH App · Apple Health and Google Fit sync · 16.5 x 41.3 in. deck · 1.25 CHP / 3.5 HP peak brushless · 12-level auto incline · 400 lb max (330 lb sustained) · 3-yr warranty",
    pros: [
      "The MERACH App gives real-time tracking and syncs with Apple Health and Google Fit, per the listing",
      "Twelve levels of automatic incline",
      "A 400 lb maximum and 330 lb recommended sustained capacity, which the listing says SGS verified",
      "A 3-year warranty, the longest stated on this page",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The listing bullets we read do not give a speed range",
      "At about $282 it costs twice the budget pick",
      "The quoted 53.6 dB average noise level is the maker’s figure",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The pad to buy if you want your walks in Apple Health or Google Fit, with incline and a sturdy frame behind it.",
    description: "The UltraWalk W60 pairs the most useful app on this page with the most solid pad. The listing says the MERACH App gives real-time fitness tracking and syncs with Apple Health and Google Fit, and the pad can also be run from a remote that docks magnetically, so the app is optional. On the pad side, the listing gives a brushless motor rated 1.25 CHP and 3.5 HP peak with Hall sensor control and dual-vent cooling, a 16.5 by 41.3-inch walking deck, 12 levels of automatic incline, a 67.7 lb steel frame, a 400 lb maximum capacity with a recommended sustained capacity of 330 lb (verified by SGS, it says), an average noise level of about 53.6 dB, a safety key with tether and a child lock, a Bluetooth speaker, customisable RGB lighting, pause memory, transport wheels and flat or upright storage. It is backed by a 3-year warranty, per the listing. The bullets we read do not state a speed range, so we have left it off; check it on the listing before you order. Plan on the 330 lb sustained figure rather than the 400 lb maximum. Amazon showed it at $282.12 on 24 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "urevo-smart-walking-pad",
    name: "UREVO Smart Walking Pad",
