      "About $133, the cheapest pick here",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Flat only, with no incline",
      "A 265 lb limit and a 39.8-inch belt suit slow walking more than a long stride",
      "The listing does not name the app or mention health-platform sync",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheapest way to get an app with routes and goals on a sensible pad, for walkers comfortably under 265 lb.",
    description: "UREVO’s Smart Walking Pad has the fullest app feature list of the budget pads we read. The listing says it links to the workout app over Bluetooth to monitor steps, distance, calories and workout time, with Track Insights to keep the data in one place, and that you can set personal goals, explore more than 50 global virtual routes, race virtual opponents in 3D environments, and use MIIT mode, preset programs, walking competitions and themed activities. It does not give the app a name beyond calling it the workout app, and it does not mention Apple Health or Google Fit. The pad works without the app: the listing describes it as plug-and-play, run from the LED display, the included remote or the app. It gives a 15 by 39.8-inch non-slip belt, a dual shock-absorption system with a 5-layer belt, 8 silicone absorbers and 2 rubber pads, a 2.5 HP motor, speeds of 0.6 to 4 mph, a 265 lb user limit and a 4.1-inch slim profile with wheels. There is no incline. Amazon showed it at $132.99 on 24 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "serenelife-handrail-app",
    name: "SereneLife Foldable Treadmill with Handrail",
    brand: "SereneLife",
    category: "Best for Zwift, Kinomap and FitShow",
    badge: "Best for Zwift and Kinomap",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H2BNL42G?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
