  },
  {
    id: "urevo-strol-2e-pro",
    name: "UREVO Strol 2E Pro",
    brand: "UREVO",
    category: "App that sets your speed for you",
    badge: "Best Automatic Speed",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H1H4JT4C?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/410e3-vj4nL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/urevo-treadmills/",
    priceRange: "About $178 (Amazon, 24 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":178,"high":178},
    specs: "Smart app with AI auto-speed · virtual trails · 0.6–4 mph walking / 0.4–6.2 mph running mode · 12% manual incline · safety handle · 44 lb",
    pros: [
      "The listing says the app reads your rhythm and adjusts speed automatically",
      "Virtual world trails and pace matched to the tempo of a playlist",
      "A walking mode to 4 mph and a running mode to 6.2 mph, plus a 12% manual incline",
      "At 44 lb, the lightest pad here, with a fold-in-seconds frame",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The app is not named, and “integrates with other apps” is not explained",
      "The listing bullets we read do not give a belt size or weight limit",
      "Automatic speed needs the app; without it this is a standard pad",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The pick if you want the app to pace your walk for you, in a light pad you can fold and wheel away.",
    description: "The Strol 2E Pro’s app does more than any other maker app here, at least on paper. The listing says its AI-driven auto-speed control reads your rhythm and fine-tunes speed, that the app offers virtual world trails with terrain replication and routes from destinations worldwide, that it can match the pad’s pace to the tempo of a playlist, and that it keeps your workout archive and integrates with other apps; it does not say which. It does not name the app beyond the UREVO brand. Without the app it runs as a normal pad: the listing title describes an LED display and plug-and-play operation, and the automatic speed is the only feature tied to the phone. The listing gives a 12% manual incline, a walking mode of 0.6 to 4 mph and a running mode of 0.4 to 6.2 mph, a SwiftFold frame that folds in seconds without tools, glide wheels, a safety handle and a weight of 44 lb. The bullets we read do not state a belt size or weight limit, so check both on the listing before ordering. Our walking pads with incline guide also covers this pad. Amazon showed it at $177.64 on 24 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "cybergoing-t10",
    name: "Cybergoing T10",
    brand: "Cybergoing",
    category: "Simple app on a Bosch-powered pad",
