          <h2>The bottom line</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">For most people the best walking pad with an app is the MERACH UltraWalk W60</strong>:
            the MERACH App tracks each walk and syncs with Apple Health and Google Fit, and the pad behind it has
            12-level auto incline, a 330 lb sustained capacity and a 3-year warranty for about $282. On a budget,
            UREVO’s Smart Walking Pad gives you an app with routes and goals for about $133; if you already use
            Zwift, Kinomap or FitShow, buy the SereneLife handrail pad, which names all three.
          </p>
          <p>
            Whichever you choose, treat the app as a bonus rather than the reason to buy. Choose the pad on its
            belt, weight limit and warranty, make sure it runs without the phone, and check that the app sends
            your walks where you want them. Our <a href="/best-walking-pads/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">best walking pads</a> guide ranks the pads themselves, and the <a href="/best-walking-pads-with-incline/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">walking pads with incline</a> guide covers the ones that tilt.
          </p>
